7080               /ON ANY ERROR, WE COME HERE.  IF THE USER THAT CAUSED THE ERROR WAS NOT
7081               /WAITING FOR THE DECTAPE, WE CLEAR HIS INPUT WAIT BIT, SET HIS ERROR BIT,
7082               /AND LEAVE.  IF HIS DECTAPE WAIT BIT IS ON, HE EITHER ALREADY HAS THE DECTAPE,
7083               /OR HE IS WAITING IN THE QUEUE.  SINCE HE IS WAITING, THE ERROR COULD ONLY
7084               /HAVE BEEN CAUSED BY AN INTERRUPT - ^C, KEYBOARD BUFFER FULL, OR THE LIKE.
7085               /IF HE IS AT THE TOP OF THE QUEUE, WE ASSUME HE HAS THE DECTAPE, AND DON'T
7086               /BOTHER WITH HIM HERE EXCEPT FOR HIS INPUT WAIT AND ERROR BITS.
7087               /IF HOWEVER, HE WAS PUT TO SLEEP BY DTGRAB, AND IS STILL WAITING TO
7088               /GET AT THE DECTAPE ROUTINE, IT WOULD BE A SHAME TO MAKE HIM WAIT FOR
7089               /ALL THE OTHER USERS AHEAD OF HIM IN THE QUEUE (WHICH COULD BE AS MANY AS
7090               /SEVEN SEEKS FROM ONE END OF THE TAPE TO THE OTHER) JUST TO FIND OUT THAT
7091               /HE WAS TRYING TO CANCEL THE OPERATION ANYWAY.  IN THAT CASE, WE TURN OFF
7092               /HIS DECTAPE WAIT BIT AND SQUISH HIM (OH - SO PAINFULLY) OUT OF THE
7093               /DECTAPE QUEUE. UNFORTUNATELY DTFREE WILL ONLY REMOVE HIM IF HE IS
7094               /ALREADY AT THE TOP OF THE QUEUE.
